---
title: Electric Collection
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electric collections provide seamless integration between TanStack DB and ElectricSQL, enabling real-time data synchronization with your Postgres database through Electric's sync engine."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/electric-db-collection"},{"type":"text","value":" package allows you to create collections that:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatically sync data from Postgres via Electric shapes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Support optimistic updates with transaction matching and automatic rollback on errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handle persistence through customizable mutation handlers"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/electric-db-collection @tanstack/react-db","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createCollection } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { electricCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\nconst todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n    },\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"electricCollectionOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts the following options:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"required-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required Options"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shapeOptions"},{"type":"text","value":": Configuration for the ElectricSQL ShapeStream"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"url"},{"type":"text","value":": The URL of your proxy to Electric"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getKey"},{"type":"text","value":": Function to extract the unique key from an item"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"optional","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":": Unique identifier for the collection"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schema"},{"type":"text","value":": Schema for validating items. Any Standard Schema compatible schema"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sync"},{"type":"text","value":": Custom sync configuration"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"persistence-handlers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence Handlers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handlers are called before mutations to persist changes to your backend:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInsert"},{"type":"text","value":": Handler called before insert operations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUpdate"},{"type":"text","value":": Handler called before update operations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onDelete"},{"type":"text","value":": Handler called before delete operations"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each handler should call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await collection.utils.awaitTxId(txid)"},{"type":"text","value":" to wait for synchronization. For cases where your API cannot return txids, use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaitMatch"},{"type":"text","value":" utility function."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"persistence-handlers-synchronization","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence Handlers & Synchronization"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handlers persist mutations to the backend and wait for Electric to sync the changes back. This prevents UI glitches where optimistic updates would be removed and then re-added. TanStack DB blocks sync data until the mutation is confirmed, ensuring smooth user experience."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-using-txid-recommended","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Using Txid (Recommended)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The recommended approach uses PostgreSQL transaction IDs (txids) for precise matching. The backend returns a txid, and the client waits for that specific txid to appear in the Electric stream."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'todos',\n    schema: todoSchema,\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n      params: { table: 'todos' },\n    },\n\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction, collection }) => {\n      const newItem = transaction.mutations[0].modified\n      const response = await api.todos.create(newItem)\n\n      // Wait for txid to sync\n      await collection.utils.awaitTxId(response.txid)\n    },\n\n    onUpdate: async ({ transaction, collection }) => {\n      const { original, changes } = transaction.mutations[0]\n      const response = await api.todos.update({\n        where: { id: original.id },\n        data: changes\n      })\n\n      // Wait for txid to sync\n      await collection.utils.awaitTxId(response.txid)\n    }\n  })\n)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-using-custom-match-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Using Custom Match Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cases where txids aren't available, use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaitMatch"},{"type":"text","value":" utility function to wait for synchronization with custom matching logic:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { isChangeMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\nconst todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'todos',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n      params: { table: 'todos' },\n    },\n\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction, collection }) => {\n      const newItem = transaction.mutations[0].modified\n      await api.todos.create(newItem)\n\n      // Use awaitMatch utility for custom matching\n      await collection.utils.awaitMatch(\n        (message) => {\n          return isChangeMessage(message) &&\n                 message.headers.operation === 'insert' &&\n                 message.value.text === newItem.text\n        },\n        5000 // timeout in ms (optional, defaults to 15000)\n      )\n    }\n  })\n)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-using-simple-timeout","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Using Simple Timeout"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For quick prototyping or when you're confident about timing, you can use a simple timeout. This is crude but works as almost always the data will be synced back in under 2 seconds:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'todos',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n      params: { table: 'todos' },\n    },\n\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      const newItem = transaction.mutations[0].modified\n      await api.todos.create(newItem)\n\n      // Simple timeout approach\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 2000))\n    }\n  })\n)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the backend, you can extract the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"txid"},{"type":"text","value":" for a transaction by querying Postgres directly."}]},{"type":"code","value":"async function generateTxId(tx) {\n  // The ::xid cast strips off the epoch, giving you the raw 32-bit value\n  // that matches what PostgreSQL sends in logical replication streams\n  // (and then exposed through Electric which we'll match against\n  // in the client).\n  const result = await tx.execute(\n    sql`SELECT pg_current_xact_id()::xid::text as txid`\n  )\n  const txid = result.rows[0]?.txid\n\n  if (txid === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Failed to get transaction ID`)\n  }\n\n  return parseInt(txid as string, 10)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"electric-proxy-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electric Proxy Example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Electric is typically deployed behind a proxy server that handles shape configuration, authentication and authorization. This provides better security and allows you to control what data users can access without exposing Electric to the client."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here is an example proxy implementation using TanStack Start:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createServerFileRoute } from \"@tanstack/react-start/server\"\nimport { ELECTRIC_PROTOCOL_QUERY_PARAMS } from \"@electric-sql/client\"\n\n// Electric URL\nconst baseUrl = 'http://.../v1/shape'\n\nconst serve = async ({ request }: { request: Request }) => {\n  // ...check user authorization  \n  const url = new URL(request.url)\n  const originUrl = new URL(baseUrl)\n\n  // passthrough parameters from electric client\n  url.searchParams.forEach((value, key) => {\n    if (ELECTRIC_PROTOCOL_QUERY_PARAMS.includes(key)) {\n      originUrl.searchParams.set(key, value)\n    }\n  })\n\n  // set shape parameters \n  // full spec: https://github.com/electric-sql/electric/blob/main/website/electric-api.yaml\n  originUrl.searchParams.set(\"table\", \"todos\")\n  // Where clause to filter rows in the table (optional).\n  // originUrl.searchParams.set(\"where\", \"completed = true\")\n  \n  // Select the columns to sync (optional)\n  // originUrl.searchParams.set(\"columns\", \"id,text,completed\")\n\n  const response = await fetch(originUrl)\n  const headers = new Headers(response.headers)\n  headers.delete(\"content-encoding\")\n  headers.delete(\"content-length\")\n\n  return new Response(response.body, {\n    status: response.status,\n    statusText: response.statusText,\n    headers,\n  })\n}\n\nexport const ServerRoute = createServerFileRoute(\"/api/todos\").methods({\n  GET: serve,\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"optimistic-updates-with-explicit-transactions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optimistic Updates with Explicit Transactions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For more advanced use cases, you can create custom actions that can do multiple mutations across collections transactionally. You can use the utility methods to wait for synchronization with different strategies:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-txid-strategy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using Txid Strategy"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const addTodoAction = createOptimisticAction({\n  onMutate: ({ text }) => {\n    // optimistically insert with a temporary ID\n    const tempId = crypto.randomUUID()\n    todosCollection.insert({\n      id: tempId,\n      text,\n      completed: false,\n      created_at: new Date(),\n    })\n    \n    // ... mutate other collections\n  },\n  \n  mutationFn: async ({ text }) => {\n    const response = await api.todos.create({\n      data: { text, completed: false }\n    })\n    \n    // Wait for the specific txid\n    await todosCollection.utils.awaitTxId(response.txid)\n  }\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-custom-match-function","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using Custom Match Function"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { isChangeMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\nconst addTodoAction = createOptimisticAction({\n  onMutate: ({ text }) => {\n    const tempId = crypto.randomUUID()\n    todosCollection.insert({\n      id: tempId,\n      text,\n      completed: false,\n      created_at: new Date(),\n    })\n  },\n  \n  mutationFn: async ({ text }) => {\n    await api.todos.create({\n      data: { text, completed: false }\n    })\n    \n    // Wait for matching message\n    await todosCollection.utils.awaitMatch(\n      (message) => {\n        return isChangeMessage(message) && \n               message.headers.operation === 'insert' &&\n               message.value.text === text\n      }\n    )\n  }\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"utility-methods","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Utility Methods"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The collection provides these utility methods via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection.utils"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"awaittxid-txid-timeout","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaitTxId(txid, timeout?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wait for a specific transaction ID to be synchronized:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Wait for specific txid\nawait todosCollection.utils.awaitTxId(12345)\n\n// With custom timeout (default is 15 seconds)\nawait todosCollection.utils.awaitTxId(12345, 10000)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is useful when you need to ensure a mutation has been synchronized before proceeding with other operations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a collection wrapped with SQLite persistence, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaitTxId"},{"type":"text","value":" observes the\ntransaction in the Electric stream. It can resolve before the local SQLite\nwrite completes. Do not use it as a local durability acknowledgment: if the\npage closes in that gap, reopening may need Electric to recover the row."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"awaitmatch-matchfn-timeout","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaitMatch(matchFn, timeout?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wait for a custom match function to find a matching message:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { isChangeMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\n// Wait for a specific message pattern\nawait todosCollection.utils.awaitMatch(\n  (message) => {\n    return isChangeMessage(message) &&\n           message.headers.operation === 'insert' &&\n           message.value.text === 'New Todo'\n  },\n  5000 // timeout in ms\n)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cleanup-and-resume-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup and resume safety"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transaction evidence and pending "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaitTxId"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaitMatch"},{"type":"text","value":" calls belong to one\ncollection lifecycle. Explicit cleanup and automatic garbage collection reject\npending waits with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamAbortedError"},{"type":"text","value":"; callbacks from the retired stream cannot\nsettle waits in a restarted collection. Observe these promises even when the\ncomponent or collection may be disposed before they settle."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persisted resumes wait for the cached row baseline to finish hydrating. If the\npersistence wrapper cannot verify hydration completion, Electric starts a fresh\nsnapshot instead of using the saved offset and handle. It warns once per options\ndescriptor; update the persistence adapter alongside Electric to enable safe resume.\nFresh eager snapshots wait for hydration, then replace the cached rows at the\nsnapshot's commit boundary. Rows omitted from that snapshot do not survive in\nthe collection or its persisted cache, even when the fresh snapshot is empty."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tag membership is kept in memory, not restored from cached row headers. A cold\nrestart therefore fetches a full snapshot when the saved state needs tags, or\ncomes from an older version that did not record whether tags were used. Untagged\nshapes can still resume from their saved offset. Cached rows remain visible until\nthe replacement snapshot completes; a partial batch or subset completion cannot\npublish that replacement early. Interrupting recovery leaves a durable reset\nmarker so the next start still refetches. This recovery also requests a full shape\nsnapshot in on-demand mode, at the cost of fetching more than the active subsets."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An eager or progressive resume cannot apply a partial update to an unknown row.\nThe adapter rejects that batch, enters an error state, and records a reset so the\nnext sync starts from a full snapshot. This does not silently retry the failed\nstream. Complete updates from an explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"replica: 'full'"},{"type":"text","value":" stream remain valid.\nOn-demand streams can observe updates outside their loaded subsets; unknown\npartial rows are ignored, while transaction acknowledgement evidence is retained.\nComplete rows published by persistence reloads or another tab are valid baselines\nfor subsequent partial updates. Pending deletions and resets still take precedence\nover an older row that remains publicly visible."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reusing Electric collection options, including a spread of those options, does\nnot share transaction waiters or tag visibility between collections. Tag state\nsurvives a compatible resume of the same collection and clears on a fresh\nsnapshot or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"must-refetch"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"helper-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helper Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The package exports helper functions for use in custom match functions:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isChangeMessage(message)"},{"type":"text","value":": Check if a message is a data change (insert/update/delete)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isControlMessage(message)"},{"type":"text","value":": Check if a message is a control message (up-to-date, must-refetch)"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { isChangeMessage, isControlMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\n// Use in custom match functions\nconst matchFn = (message) => {\n  if (isChangeMessage(message)) {\n    return message.headers.operation === 'insert'\n  }\n  return false\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"debugging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"common-issue-awaittxid-stalls-or-times-out","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Issue: awaitTxId Stalls or Times Out"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A frequent issue developers encounter is that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaitTxId"},{"type":"text","value":" (or the transaction's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPersisted.promise"},{"type":"text","value":") stalls indefinitely, eventually timing out with no error messages. The data persists correctly to the database, but the optimistic mutation never resolves."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Root Cause:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" This happens when the transaction ID (txid) returned from your API doesn't match the actual transaction ID of the mutation in Postgres. This mismatch occurs when you query "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pg_current_xact_id()"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"outside"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the same transaction that performs the mutation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enable-debug-logging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable Debug Logging"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To diagnose txid issues, enable debug logging in your browser console:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"localStorage.debug = 'ts/db:electric'","lang":"javascript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This will show you when mutations start waiting for txids and when txids arrive from Electric's sync stream."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is powered by the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/debug","children":[{"type":"text","value":"debug"}]},{"type":"text","value":" package."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When txids DON'T match (common bug):"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"ts/db:electric awaitTxId called with txid 124\nts/db:electric new txids synced from pg [123]\n// Stalls forever - 124 never arrives!"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this example, the mutation happened in transaction 123, but you queried "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pg_current_xact_id()"},{"type":"text","value":" in a separate transaction (124) that ran after the mutation. The client waits for 124 which will never arrive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When txids DO match (correct):"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"ts/db:electric awaitTxId called with txid 123\nts/db:electric new txids synced from pg [123]\nts/db:electric awaitTxId found match for txid 123\n// Resolves immediately!"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"the-solution-query-txid-inside-the-transaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Solution: Query txid Inside the Transaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"must"}]},{"type":"text","value":" call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pg_current_xact_id()"},{"type":"text","value":" inside the same transaction as your mutation:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❌ Wrong - txid queried outside transaction:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// DON'T DO THIS\nasync function createTodo(data) {\n  const txid = await generateTxId(sql) // Wrong: separate transaction\n\n  await sql.begin(async (tx) => {\n    await tx`INSERT INTO todos ${tx(data)}`\n  })\n\n  return { txid } // This txid won't match!\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ Correct - txid queried inside transaction:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// DO THIS\nasync function createTodo(data) {\n  let txid!: Txid\n\n  const result = await sql.begin(async (tx) => {\n    // Call generateTxId INSIDE the transaction\n    txid = await generateTxId(tx)\n\n    const [todo] = await tx`\n      INSERT INTO todos ${tx(data)}\n      RETURNING *\n    `\n    return todo\n  })\n\n  return { todo: result, txid } // txid matches the mutation\n}\n\nasync function generateTxId(tx: any): Promise<Txid> {\n  const result = await tx`SELECT pg_current_xact_id()::xid::text as txid`\n  const txid = result[0]?.txid\n\n  if (txid === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Failed to get transaction ID`)\n  }\n\n  return parseInt(txid, 10)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See working examples in:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/react/todo/src/routes/api/todos.ts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/react/todo/src/api/server.ts"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"configuration-options","text":"Configuration Options","level":2},{"id":"required-options","text":"Required Options","level":3},{"id":"optional","text":"Optional","level":3},{"id":"persistence-handlers","text":"Persistence Handlers","level":3},{"id":"persistence-handlers-synchronization","text":"Persistence Handlers & Synchronization","level":2},{"id":"1-using-txid-recommended","text":"1. Using Txid (Recommended)","level":3},{"id":"2-using-custom-match-functions","text":"2. Using Custom Match Functions","level":3},{"id":"3-using-simple-timeout","text":"3. Using Simple Timeout","level":3},{"id":"electric-proxy-example","text":"Electric Proxy Example","level":3},{"id":"optimistic-updates-with-explicit-transactions","text":"Optimistic Updates with Explicit Transactions","level":2},{"id":"using-txid-strategy","text":"Using Txid Strategy","level":3},{"id":"using-custom-match-function","text":"Using Custom Match Function","level":3},{"id":"utility-methods","text":"Utility Methods","level":2},{"id":"awaittxid-txid-timeout","text":"awaitTxId(txid, timeout?)","level":3},{"id":"awaitmatch-matchfn-timeout","text":"awaitMatch(matchFn, timeout?)","level":3},{"id":"cleanup-and-resume-safety","text":"Cleanup and resume safety","level":3},{"id":"helper-functions","text":"Helper Functions","level":3},{"id":"debugging","text":"Debugging","level":2},{"id":"common-issue-awaittxid-stalls-or-times-out","text":"Common Issue: awaitTxId Stalls or Times Out","level":3},{"id":"enable-debug-logging","text":"Enable Debug Logging","level":3},{"id":"the-solution-query-txid-inside-the-transaction","text":"The Solution: Query txid Inside the Transaction","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nElectric collections provide seamless integration between TanStack DB and ElectricSQL, enabling real-time data synchronization with your Postgres database through Electric's sync engine.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe `@tanstack/electric-db-collection` package allows you to create collections that:\n- Automatically sync data from Postgres via Electric shapes\n- Support optimistic updates with transaction matching and automatic rollback on errors\n- Handle persistence through customizable mutation handlers\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/electric-db-collection @tanstack/react-db\n```\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCollection } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { electricCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\nconst todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n    },\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)\n```\n\n## Configuration Options\n\nThe `electricCollectionOptions` function accepts the following options:\n\n### Required Options\n\n- `shapeOptions`: Configuration for the ElectricSQL ShapeStream\n  - `url`: The URL of your proxy to Electric\n\n- `getKey`: Function to extract the unique key from an item\n\n### Optional\n\n- `id`: Unique identifier for the collection\n- `schema`: Schema for validating items. Any Standard Schema compatible schema\n- `sync`: Custom sync configuration\n\n### Persistence Handlers\n\nHandlers are called before mutations to persist changes to your backend:\n\n- `onInsert`: Handler called before insert operations\n- `onUpdate`: Handler called before update operations\n- `onDelete`: Handler called before delete operations\n\nEach handler should call `await collection.utils.awaitTxId(txid)` to wait for synchronization. For cases where your API cannot return txids, use the `awaitMatch` utility function.\n\n## Persistence Handlers & Synchronization\n\nHandlers persist mutations to the backend and wait for Electric to sync the changes back. This prevents UI glitches where optimistic updates would be removed and then re-added. TanStack DB blocks sync data until the mutation is confirmed, ensuring smooth user experience.\n\n### 1. Using Txid (Recommended)\n\nThe recommended approach uses PostgreSQL transaction IDs (txids) for precise matching. The backend returns a txid, and the client waits for that specific txid to appear in the Electric stream.\n\n```typescript\nconst todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'todos',\n    schema: todoSchema,\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n      params: { table: 'todos' },\n    },\n\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction, collection }) => {\n      const newItem = transaction.mutations[0].modified\n      const response = await api.todos.create(newItem)\n\n      // Wait for txid to sync\n      await collection.utils.awaitTxId(response.txid)\n    },\n\n    onUpdate: async ({ transaction, collection }) => {\n      const { original, changes } = transaction.mutations[0]\n      const response = await api.todos.update({\n        where: { id: original.id },\n        data: changes\n      })\n\n      // Wait for txid to sync\n      await collection.utils.awaitTxId(response.txid)\n    }\n  })\n)\n```\n\n### 2. Using Custom Match Functions\n\nFor cases where txids aren't available, use the `awaitMatch` utility function to wait for synchronization with custom matching logic:\n\n```typescript\nimport { isChangeMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\nconst todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'todos',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n      params: { table: 'todos' },\n    },\n\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction, collection }) => {\n      const newItem = transaction.mutations[0].modified\n      await api.todos.create(newItem)\n\n      // Use awaitMatch utility for custom matching\n      await collection.utils.awaitMatch(\n        (message) => {\n          return isChangeMessage(message) &&\n                 message.headers.operation === 'insert' &&\n                 message.value.text === newItem.text\n        },\n        5000 // timeout in ms (optional, defaults to 15000)\n      )\n    }\n  })\n)\n```\n\n### 3. Using Simple Timeout\n\nFor quick prototyping or when you're confident about timing, you can use a simple timeout. This is crude but works as almost always the data will be synced back in under 2 seconds:\n\n```typescript\nconst todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'todos',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n      params: { table: 'todos' },\n    },\n\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      const newItem = transaction.mutations[0].modified\n      await api.todos.create(newItem)\n\n      // Simple timeout approach\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 2000))\n    }\n  })\n)\n```\n\nOn the backend, you can extract the `txid` for a transaction by querying Postgres directly.\n\n```ts\nasync function generateTxId(tx) {\n  // The ::xid cast strips off the epoch, giving you the raw 32-bit value\n  // that matches what PostgreSQL sends in logical replication streams\n  // (and then exposed through Electric which we'll match against\n  // in the client).\n  const result = await tx.execute(\n    sql`SELECT pg_current_xact_id()::xid::text as txid`\n  )\n  const txid = result.rows[0]?.txid\n\n  if (txid === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Failed to get transaction ID`)\n  }\n\n  return parseInt(txid as string, 10)\n}\n```\n\n### Electric Proxy Example\n\nElectric is typically deployed behind a proxy server that handles shape configuration, authentication and authorization. This provides better security and allows you to control what data users can access without exposing Electric to the client.\n\n\nHere is an example proxy implementation using TanStack Start:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createServerFileRoute } from \"@tanstack/react-start/server\"\nimport { ELECTRIC_PROTOCOL_QUERY_PARAMS } from \"@electric-sql/client\"\n\n// Electric URL\nconst baseUrl = 'http://.../v1/shape'\n\nconst serve = async ({ request }: { request: Request }) => {\n  // ...check user authorization  \n  const url = new URL(request.url)\n  const originUrl = new URL(baseUrl)\n\n  // passthrough parameters from electric client\n  url.searchParams.forEach((value, key) => {\n    if (ELECTRIC_PROTOCOL_QUERY_PARAMS.includes(key)) {\n      originUrl.searchParams.set(key, value)\n    }\n  })\n\n  // set shape parameters \n  // full spec: https://github.com/electric-sql/electric/blob/main/website/electric-api.yaml\n  originUrl.searchParams.set(\"table\", \"todos\")\n  // Where clause to filter rows in the table (optional).\n  // originUrl.searchParams.set(\"where\", \"completed = true\")\n  \n  // Select the columns to sync (optional)\n  // originUrl.searchParams.set(\"columns\", \"id,text,completed\")\n\n  const response = await fetch(originUrl)\n  const headers = new Headers(response.headers)\n  headers.delete(\"content-encoding\")\n  headers.delete(\"content-length\")\n\n  return new Response(response.body, {\n    status: response.status,\n    statusText: response.statusText,\n    headers,\n  })\n}\n\nexport const ServerRoute = createServerFileRoute(\"/api/todos\").methods({\n  GET: serve,\n})\n```\n\n## Optimistic Updates with Explicit Transactions\n\nFor more advanced use cases, you can create custom actions that can do multiple mutations across collections transactionally. You can use the utility methods to wait for synchronization with different strategies:\n\n### Using Txid Strategy\n\n```typescript\nconst addTodoAction = createOptimisticAction({\n  onMutate: ({ text }) => {\n    // optimistically insert with a temporary ID\n    const tempId = crypto.randomUUID()\n    todosCollection.insert({\n      id: tempId,\n      text,\n      completed: false,\n      created_at: new Date(),\n    })\n    \n    // ... mutate other collections\n  },\n  \n  mutationFn: async ({ text }) => {\n    const response = await api.todos.create({\n      data: { text, completed: false }\n    })\n    \n    // Wait for the specific txid\n    await todosCollection.utils.awaitTxId(response.txid)\n  }\n})\n```\n\n### Using Custom Match Function\n\n```typescript\nimport { isChangeMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\nconst addTodoAction = createOptimisticAction({\n  onMutate: ({ text }) => {\n    const tempId = crypto.randomUUID()\n    todosCollection.insert({\n      id: tempId,\n      text,\n      completed: false,\n      created_at: new Date(),\n    })\n  },\n  \n  mutationFn: async ({ text }) => {\n    await api.todos.create({\n      data: { text, completed: false }\n    })\n    \n    // Wait for matching message\n    await todosCollection.utils.awaitMatch(\n      (message) => {\n        return isChangeMessage(message) && \n               message.headers.operation === 'insert' &&\n               message.value.text === text\n      }\n    )\n  }\n})\n```\n\n## Utility Methods\n\nThe collection provides these utility methods via `collection.utils`:\n\n### `awaitTxId(txid, timeout?)`\n\nWait for a specific transaction ID to be synchronized:\n\n```typescript\n// Wait for specific txid\nawait todosCollection.utils.awaitTxId(12345)\n\n// With custom timeout (default is 15 seconds)\nawait todosCollection.utils.awaitTxId(12345, 10000)\n```\n\nThis is useful when you need to ensure a mutation has been synchronized before proceeding with other operations.\n\nFor a collection wrapped with SQLite persistence, `awaitTxId` observes the\ntransaction in the Electric stream. It can resolve before the local SQLite\nwrite completes. Do not use it as a local durability acknowledgment: if the\npage closes in that gap, reopening may need Electric to recover the row.\n\n### `awaitMatch(matchFn, timeout?)`\n\nWait for a custom match function to find a matching message:\n\n```typescript\nimport { isChangeMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\n// Wait for a specific message pattern\nawait todosCollection.utils.awaitMatch(\n  (message) => {\n    return isChangeMessage(message) &&\n           message.headers.operation === 'insert' &&\n           message.value.text === 'New Todo'\n  },\n  5000 // timeout in ms\n)\n```\n\n### Cleanup and resume safety\n\nTransaction evidence and pending `awaitTxId`/`awaitMatch` calls belong to one\ncollection lifecycle. Explicit cleanup and automatic garbage collection reject\npending waits with `StreamAbortedError`; callbacks from the retired stream cannot\nsettle waits in a restarted collection. Observe these promises even when the\ncomponent or collection may be disposed before they settle.\n\nPersisted resumes wait for the cached row baseline to finish hydrating. If the\npersistence wrapper cannot verify hydration completion, Electric starts a fresh\nsnapshot instead of using the saved offset and handle. It warns once per options\ndescriptor; update the persistence adapter alongside Electric to enable safe resume.\nFresh eager snapshots wait for hydration, then replace the cached rows at the\nsnapshot's commit boundary. Rows omitted from that snapshot do not survive in\nthe collection or its persisted cache, even when the fresh snapshot is empty.\n\nTag membership is kept in memory, not restored from cached row headers. A cold\nrestart therefore fetches a full snapshot when the saved state needs tags, or\ncomes from an older version that did not record whether tags were used. Untagged\nshapes can still resume from their saved offset. Cached rows remain visible until\nthe replacement snapshot completes; a partial batch or subset completion cannot\npublish that replacement early. Interrupting recovery leaves a durable reset\nmarker so the next start still refetches. This recovery also requests a full shape\nsnapshot in on-demand mode, at the cost of fetching more than the active subsets.\n\nAn eager or progressive resume cannot apply a partial update to an unknown row.\nThe adapter rejects that batch, enters an error state, and records a reset so the\nnext sync starts from a full snapshot. This does not silently retry the failed\nstream. Complete updates from an explicit `replica: 'full'` stream remain valid.\nOn-demand streams can observe updates outside their loaded subsets; unknown\npartial rows are ignored, while transaction acknowledgement evidence is retained.\nComplete rows published by persistence reloads or another tab are valid baselines\nfor subsequent partial updates. Pending deletions and resets still take precedence\nover an older row that remains publicly visible.\n\nReusing Electric collection options, including a spread of those options, does\nnot share transaction waiters or tag visibility between collections. Tag state\nsurvives a compatible resume of the same collection and clears on a fresh\nsnapshot or `must-refetch`.\n\n### Helper Functions\n\nThe package exports helper functions for use in custom match functions:\n\n- `isChangeMessage(message)`: Check if a message is a data change (insert/update/delete)\n- `isControlMessage(message)`: Check if a message is a control message (up-to-date, must-refetch)\n\n```typescript\nimport { isChangeMessage, isControlMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\n// Use in custom match functions\nconst matchFn = (message) => {\n  if (isChangeMessage(message)) {\n    return message.headers.operation === 'insert'\n  }\n  return false\n}\n```\n\n## Debugging\n\n### Common Issue: awaitTxId Stalls or Times Out\n\nA frequent issue developers encounter is that `awaitTxId` (or the transaction's `isPersisted.promise`) stalls indefinitely, eventually timing out with no error messages. The data persists correctly to the database, but the optimistic mutation never resolves.\n\n**Root Cause:** This happens when the transaction ID (txid) returned from your API doesn't match the actual transaction ID of the mutation in Postgres. This mismatch occurs when you query `pg_current_xact_id()` **outside** the same transaction that performs the mutation.\n\n### Enable Debug Logging\n\nTo diagnose txid issues, enable debug logging in your browser console:\n\n```javascript\nlocalStorage.debug = 'ts/db:electric'\n```\n\nThis will show you when mutations start waiting for txids and when txids arrive from Electric's sync stream.\n\nThis is powered by the [debug](https://www.npmjs.com/package/debug) package.\n\n**When txids DON'T match (common bug):**\n```\nts/db:electric awaitTxId called with txid 124\nts/db:electric new txids synced from pg [123]\n// Stalls forever - 124 never arrives!\n```\n\nIn this example, the mutation happened in transaction 123, but you queried `pg_current_xact_id()` in a separate transaction (124) that ran after the mutation. The client waits for 124 which will never arrive.\n\n**When txids DO match (correct):**\n```\nts/db:electric awaitTxId called with txid 123\nts/db:electric new txids synced from pg [123]\nts/db:electric awaitTxId found match for txid 123\n// Resolves immediately!\n```\n\n### The Solution: Query txid Inside the Transaction\n\nYou **must** call `pg_current_xact_id()` inside the same transaction as your mutation:\n\n**❌ Wrong - txid queried outside transaction:**\n```typescript\n// DON'T DO THIS\nasync function createTodo(data) {\n  const txid = await generateTxId(sql) // Wrong: separate transaction\n\n  await sql.begin(async (tx) => {\n    await tx`INSERT INTO todos ${tx(data)}`\n  })\n\n  return { txid } // This txid won't match!\n}\n```\n\n**✅ Correct - txid queried inside transaction:**\n```typescript\n// DO THIS\nasync function createTodo(data) {\n  let txid!: Txid\n\n  const result = await sql.begin(async (tx) => {\n    // Call generateTxId INSIDE the transaction\n    txid = await generateTxId(tx)\n\n    const [todo] = await tx`\n      INSERT INTO todos ${tx(data)}\n      RETURNING *\n    `\n    return todo\n  })\n\n  return { todo: result, txid } // txid matches the mutation\n}\n\nasync function generateTxId(tx: any): Promise<Txid> {\n  const result = await tx`SELECT pg_current_xact_id()::xid::text as txid`\n  const txid = result[0]?.txid\n\n  if (txid === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Failed to get transaction ID`)\n  }\n\n  return parseInt(txid, 10)\n}\n```\n\nSee working examples in:\n- `examples/react/todo/src/routes/api/todos.ts`\n- `examples/react/todo/src/api/server.ts`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Electric Collection\n---\n\nElectric collections provide seamless integration between TanStack DB and ElectricSQL, enabling real-time data synchronization with your Postgres database through Electric's sync engine.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe `@tanstack/electric-db-collection` package allows you to create collections that:\n- Automatically sync data from Postgres via Electric shapes\n- Support optimistic updates with transaction matching and automatic rollback on errors\n- Handle persistence through customizable mutation handlers\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/electric-db-collection @tanstack/react-db\n```\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCollection } from '@tanstack/react-db'\nimport { electricCollectionOptions } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\nconst todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n    },\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n  })\n)\n```\n\n## Configuration Options\n\nThe `electricCollectionOptions` function accepts the following options:\n\n### Required Options\n\n- `shapeOptions`: Configuration for the ElectricSQL ShapeStream\n  - `url`: The URL of your proxy to Electric\n\n- `getKey`: Function to extract the unique key from an item\n\n### Optional\n\n- `id`: Unique identifier for the collection\n- `schema`: Schema for validating items. Any Standard Schema compatible schema\n- `sync`: Custom sync configuration\n\n### Persistence Handlers\n\nHandlers are called before mutations to persist changes to your backend:\n\n- `onInsert`: Handler called before insert operations\n- `onUpdate`: Handler called before update operations\n- `onDelete`: Handler called before delete operations\n\nEach handler should call `await collection.utils.awaitTxId(txid)` to wait for synchronization. For cases where your API cannot return txids, use the `awaitMatch` utility function.\n\n## Persistence Handlers & Synchronization\n\nHandlers persist mutations to the backend and wait for Electric to sync the changes back. This prevents UI glitches where optimistic updates would be removed and then re-added. TanStack DB blocks sync data until the mutation is confirmed, ensuring smooth user experience.\n\n### 1. Using Txid (Recommended)\n\nThe recommended approach uses PostgreSQL transaction IDs (txids) for precise matching. The backend returns a txid, and the client waits for that specific txid to appear in the Electric stream.\n\n```typescript\nconst todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'todos',\n    schema: todoSchema,\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n      params: { table: 'todos' },\n    },\n\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction, collection }) => {\n      const newItem = transaction.mutations[0].modified\n      const response = await api.todos.create(newItem)\n\n      // Wait for txid to sync\n      await collection.utils.awaitTxId(response.txid)\n    },\n\n    onUpdate: async ({ transaction, collection }) => {\n      const { original, changes } = transaction.mutations[0]\n      const response = await api.todos.update({\n        where: { id: original.id },\n        data: changes\n      })\n\n      // Wait for txid to sync\n      await collection.utils.awaitTxId(response.txid)\n    }\n  })\n)\n```\n\n### 2. Using Custom Match Functions\n\nFor cases where txids aren't available, use the `awaitMatch` utility function to wait for synchronization with custom matching logic:\n\n```typescript\nimport { isChangeMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\nconst todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'todos',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n      params: { table: 'todos' },\n    },\n\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction, collection }) => {\n      const newItem = transaction.mutations[0].modified\n      await api.todos.create(newItem)\n\n      // Use awaitMatch utility for custom matching\n      await collection.utils.awaitMatch(\n        (message) => {\n          return isChangeMessage(message) &&\n                 message.headers.operation === 'insert' &&\n                 message.value.text === newItem.text\n        },\n        5000 // timeout in ms (optional, defaults to 15000)\n      )\n    }\n  })\n)\n```\n\n### 3. Using Simple Timeout\n\nFor quick prototyping or when you're confident about timing, you can use a simple timeout. This is crude but works as almost always the data will be synced back in under 2 seconds:\n\n```typescript\nconst todosCollection = createCollection(\n  electricCollectionOptions({\n    id: 'todos',\n    getKey: (item) => item.id,\n    shapeOptions: {\n      url: '/api/todos',\n      params: { table: 'todos' },\n    },\n\n    onInsert: async ({ transaction }) => {\n      const newItem = transaction.mutations[0].modified\n      await api.todos.create(newItem)\n\n      // Simple timeout approach\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 2000))\n    }\n  })\n)\n```\n\nOn the backend, you can extract the `txid` for a transaction by querying Postgres directly.\n\n```ts\nasync function generateTxId(tx) {\n  // The ::xid cast strips off the epoch, giving you the raw 32-bit value\n  // that matches what PostgreSQL sends in logical replication streams\n  // (and then exposed through Electric which we'll match against\n  // in the client).\n  const result = await tx.execute(\n    sql`SELECT pg_current_xact_id()::xid::text as txid`\n  )\n  const txid = result.rows[0]?.txid\n\n  if (txid === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Failed to get transaction ID`)\n  }\n\n  return parseInt(txid as string, 10)\n}\n```\n\n### Electric Proxy Example\n\nElectric is typically deployed behind a proxy server that handles shape configuration, authentication and authorization. This provides better security and allows you to control what data users can access without exposing Electric to the client.\n\n\nHere is an example proxy implementation using TanStack Start:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createServerFileRoute } from \"@tanstack/react-start/server\"\nimport { ELECTRIC_PROTOCOL_QUERY_PARAMS } from \"@electric-sql/client\"\n\n// Electric URL\nconst baseUrl = 'http://.../v1/shape'\n\nconst serve = async ({ request }: { request: Request }) => {\n  // ...check user authorization  \n  const url = new URL(request.url)\n  const originUrl = new URL(baseUrl)\n\n  // passthrough parameters from electric client\n  url.searchParams.forEach((value, key) => {\n    if (ELECTRIC_PROTOCOL_QUERY_PARAMS.includes(key)) {\n      originUrl.searchParams.set(key, value)\n    }\n  })\n\n  // set shape parameters \n  // full spec: https://github.com/electric-sql/electric/blob/main/website/electric-api.yaml\n  originUrl.searchParams.set(\"table\", \"todos\")\n  // Where clause to filter rows in the table (optional).\n  // originUrl.searchParams.set(\"where\", \"completed = true\")\n  \n  // Select the columns to sync (optional)\n  // originUrl.searchParams.set(\"columns\", \"id,text,completed\")\n\n  const response = await fetch(originUrl)\n  const headers = new Headers(response.headers)\n  headers.delete(\"content-encoding\")\n  headers.delete(\"content-length\")\n\n  return new Response(response.body, {\n    status: response.status,\n    statusText: response.statusText,\n    headers,\n  })\n}\n\nexport const ServerRoute = createServerFileRoute(\"/api/todos\").methods({\n  GET: serve,\n})\n```\n\n## Optimistic Updates with Explicit Transactions\n\nFor more advanced use cases, you can create custom actions that can do multiple mutations across collections transactionally. You can use the utility methods to wait for synchronization with different strategies:\n\n### Using Txid Strategy\n\n```typescript\nconst addTodoAction = createOptimisticAction({\n  onMutate: ({ text }) => {\n    // optimistically insert with a temporary ID\n    const tempId = crypto.randomUUID()\n    todosCollection.insert({\n      id: tempId,\n      text,\n      completed: false,\n      created_at: new Date(),\n    })\n    \n    // ... mutate other collections\n  },\n  \n  mutationFn: async ({ text }) => {\n    const response = await api.todos.create({\n      data: { text, completed: false }\n    })\n    \n    // Wait for the specific txid\n    await todosCollection.utils.awaitTxId(response.txid)\n  }\n})\n```\n\n### Using Custom Match Function\n\n```typescript\nimport { isChangeMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\nconst addTodoAction = createOptimisticAction({\n  onMutate: ({ text }) => {\n    const tempId = crypto.randomUUID()\n    todosCollection.insert({\n      id: tempId,\n      text,\n      completed: false,\n      created_at: new Date(),\n    })\n  },\n  \n  mutationFn: async ({ text }) => {\n    await api.todos.create({\n      data: { text, completed: false }\n    })\n    \n    // Wait for matching message\n    await todosCollection.utils.awaitMatch(\n      (message) => {\n        return isChangeMessage(message) && \n               message.headers.operation === 'insert' &&\n               message.value.text === text\n      }\n    )\n  }\n})\n```\n\n## Utility Methods\n\nThe collection provides these utility methods via `collection.utils`:\n\n### `awaitTxId(txid, timeout?)`\n\nWait for a specific transaction ID to be synchronized:\n\n```typescript\n// Wait for specific txid\nawait todosCollection.utils.awaitTxId(12345)\n\n// With custom timeout (default is 15 seconds)\nawait todosCollection.utils.awaitTxId(12345, 10000)\n```\n\nThis is useful when you need to ensure a mutation has been synchronized before proceeding with other operations.\n\nFor a collection wrapped with SQLite persistence, `awaitTxId` observes the\ntransaction in the Electric stream. It can resolve before the local SQLite\nwrite completes. Do not use it as a local durability acknowledgment: if the\npage closes in that gap, reopening may need Electric to recover the row.\n\n### `awaitMatch(matchFn, timeout?)`\n\nWait for a custom match function to find a matching message:\n\n```typescript\nimport { isChangeMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\n// Wait for a specific message pattern\nawait todosCollection.utils.awaitMatch(\n  (message) => {\n    return isChangeMessage(message) &&\n           message.headers.operation === 'insert' &&\n           message.value.text === 'New Todo'\n  },\n  5000 // timeout in ms\n)\n```\n\n### Cleanup and resume safety\n\nTransaction evidence and pending `awaitTxId`/`awaitMatch` calls belong to one\ncollection lifecycle. Explicit cleanup and automatic garbage collection reject\npending waits with `StreamAbortedError`; callbacks from the retired stream cannot\nsettle waits in a restarted collection. Observe these promises even when the\ncomponent or collection may be disposed before they settle.\n\nPersisted resumes wait for the cached row baseline to finish hydrating. If the\npersistence wrapper cannot verify hydration completion, Electric starts a fresh\nsnapshot instead of using the saved offset and handle. It warns once per options\ndescriptor; update the persistence adapter alongside Electric to enable safe resume.\nFresh eager snapshots wait for hydration, then replace the cached rows at the\nsnapshot's commit boundary. Rows omitted from that snapshot do not survive in\nthe collection or its persisted cache, even when the fresh snapshot is empty.\n\nTag membership is kept in memory, not restored from cached row headers. A cold\nrestart therefore fetches a full snapshot when the saved state needs tags, or\ncomes from an older version that did not record whether tags were used. Untagged\nshapes can still resume from their saved offset. Cached rows remain visible until\nthe replacement snapshot completes; a partial batch or subset completion cannot\npublish that replacement early. Interrupting recovery leaves a durable reset\nmarker so the next start still refetches. This recovery also requests a full shape\nsnapshot in on-demand mode, at the cost of fetching more than the active subsets.\n\nAn eager or progressive resume cannot apply a partial update to an unknown row.\nThe adapter rejects that batch, enters an error state, and records a reset so the\nnext sync starts from a full snapshot. This does not silently retry the failed\nstream. Complete updates from an explicit `replica: 'full'` stream remain valid.\nOn-demand streams can observe updates outside their loaded subsets; unknown\npartial rows are ignored, while transaction acknowledgement evidence is retained.\nComplete rows published by persistence reloads or another tab are valid baselines\nfor subsequent partial updates. Pending deletions and resets still take precedence\nover an older row that remains publicly visible.\n\nReusing Electric collection options, including a spread of those options, does\nnot share transaction waiters or tag visibility between collections. Tag state\nsurvives a compatible resume of the same collection and clears on a fresh\nsnapshot or `must-refetch`.\n\n### Helper Functions\n\nThe package exports helper functions for use in custom match functions:\n\n- `isChangeMessage(message)`: Check if a message is a data change (insert/update/delete)\n- `isControlMessage(message)`: Check if a message is a control message (up-to-date, must-refetch)\n\n```typescript\nimport { isChangeMessage, isControlMessage } from '@tanstack/electric-db-collection'\n\n// Use in custom match functions\nconst matchFn = (message) => {\n  if (isChangeMessage(message)) {\n    return message.headers.operation === 'insert'\n  }\n  return false\n}\n```\n\n## Debugging\n\n### Common Issue: awaitTxId Stalls or Times Out\n\nA frequent issue developers encounter is that `awaitTxId` (or the transaction's `isPersisted.promise`) stalls indefinitely, eventually timing out with no error messages. The data persists correctly to the database, but the optimistic mutation never resolves.\n\n**Root Cause:** This happens when the transaction ID (txid) returned from your API doesn't match the actual transaction ID of the mutation in Postgres. This mismatch occurs when you query `pg_current_xact_id()` **outside** the same transaction that performs the mutation.\n\n### Enable Debug Logging\n\nTo diagnose txid issues, enable debug logging in your browser console:\n\n```javascript\nlocalStorage.debug = 'ts/db:electric'\n```\n\nThis will show you when mutations start waiting for txids and when txids arrive from Electric's sync stream.\n\nThis is powered by the [debug](https://www.npmjs.com/package/debug) package.\n\n**When txids DON'T match (common bug):**\n```\nts/db:electric awaitTxId called with txid 124\nts/db:electric new txids synced from pg [123]\n// Stalls forever - 124 never arrives!\n```\n\nIn this example, the mutation happened in transaction 123, but you queried `pg_current_xact_id()` in a separate transaction (124) that ran after the mutation. The client waits for 124 which will never arrive.\n\n**When txids DO match (correct):**\n```\nts/db:electric awaitTxId called with txid 123\nts/db:electric new txids synced from pg [123]\nts/db:electric awaitTxId found match for txid 123\n// Resolves immediately!\n```\n\n### The Solution: Query txid Inside the Transaction\n\nYou **must** call `pg_current_xact_id()` inside the same transaction as your mutation:\n\n**❌ Wrong - txid queried outside transaction:**\n```typescript\n// DON'T DO THIS\nasync function createTodo(data) {\n  const txid = await generateTxId(sql) // Wrong: separate transaction\n\n  await sql.begin(async (tx) => {\n    await tx`INSERT INTO todos ${tx(data)}`\n  })\n\n  return { txid } // This txid won't match!\n}\n```\n\n**✅ Correct - txid queried inside transaction:**\n```typescript\n// DO THIS\nasync function createTodo(data) {\n  let txid!: Txid\n\n  const result = await sql.begin(async (tx) => {\n    // Call generateTxId INSIDE the transaction\n    txid = await generateTxId(tx)\n\n    const [todo] = await tx`\n      INSERT INTO todos ${tx(data)}\n      RETURNING *\n    `\n    return todo\n  })\n\n  return { todo: result, txid } // txid matches the mutation\n}\n\nasync function generateTxId(tx: any): Promise<Txid> {\n  const result = await tx`SELECT pg_current_xact_id()::xid::text as txid`\n  const txid = result[0]?.txid\n\n  if (txid === undefined) {\n    throw new Error(`Failed to get transaction ID`)\n  }\n\n  return parseInt(txid, 10)\n}\n```\n\nSee working examples in:\n- `examples/react/todo/src/routes/api/todos.ts`\n- `examples/react/todo/src/api/server.ts`\n"}
